{# The admin bar (decision-30): one template, drawn on every signed-in admin
   screen and across the top of every public page a signed-in user reads.

   It keeps to a declarative shadow root: no selector of a site theme or of
   the admin's DaisyUI theme reaches the markup inside, and the stylesheet
   inside, static/admin-bar.css, reaches nothing outside. That stylesheet is
   inlined so the bar is never drawn unstyled.

   What each place passes it:
   - `siteHref` and `barLinks`, chosen by each place for itself: the admin's
     title leads to the dashboard, the public site's home (TASK-257).
   - `me`, `logoutUrl` and `csrfToken`, for the account menu that ends it.
   - `barScheme`, `adminColorScheme` of the user's admin theme: `light` or
     `dark` is put on the host as data-scheme and pins the palette, and `auto`
     puts nothing there, so the bar follows prefers-color-scheme.
   - `cspNonce`, on the admin only. Its CSP refuses an unnonced <style> and
     any style attribute, so there the stylesheet carries the nonce and the
     host is placed by the stylesheet's :host rule alone. The public site has
     no content policy, and its host also carries that placement as a style
     attribute, which outranks a theme's rules for the element: only an
     `!important` rule can move it, which is also how a theme that insists
     hides it.
   - `assetPrefix`, where static/admin-bar.js is served from.

   WordPress's "Howdy," menu, greeting the way this site's owner does. A
   popover rather than a script: the browser opens and closes it, shuts it on
   Escape or a click elsewhere, and tells a screen reader whether it is
   expanded. #}
<geekity-admin-bar
  {%- if barScheme == 'light' or barScheme == 'dark' %} data-scheme="{{ barScheme }}"{% endif %}
  {%- if not cspNonce %} style="all: initial; display: block; position: fixed; top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; z-index: 99999"{% endif %}><template shadowrootmode="open"><style{% if cspNonce %} nonce="{{ cspNonce }}"{% endif %}>{% include "static/admin-bar.css" %}</style>
<nav class="admin-bar" aria-label="Admin bar">
  <a class="admin-bar-site" href="{{ siteHref }}">{{ site.title }}</a>
  {% for link in barLinks %}
    <a href="{{ link.url }}">{{ link.label }}</a>
  {% endfor %}
  <span class="admin-bar-spacer"></span>
  {% if me %}
    <button type="button" class="admin-bar-account" popovertarget="admin-account-menu">Hoopla! {{ me.name }}</button>
    <div id="admin-account-menu" class="admin-account-menu" popover>
      <a href="{{ me.url }}">Edit profile</a>
      <form method="post" action="{{ logoutUrl }}">
        <input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="{{ csrfToken }}" />
        <button type="submit">Log out</button>
      </form>
    </div>
  {% endif %}
</nav>
<script src="{{ assetPrefix }}admin-bar.js" defer></script></template></geekity-admin-bar>
